"""Regenerate the data-driven figures in docs/paper.md from tracked sources.

Every empirical figure in the paper is a ```latex fence written between a pair of markers:

    <!-- BEGIN GENERATED figure:NAME rev:REVISION — regenerated by scripts/paper_figures.py -->
    ...the figure, as pgfplots/TikZ with its data inlined...
    <!-- END GENERATED figure:NAME -->

This script recomputes each block from the repository's own tracked records and nothing
else -- the stress record, the Qwen storm extraction, the QwenStorm 3.0.0 evidence ledger,
the host benchmark, the delivery-estimate ledger, the test-time evidence, and the git history
read at the revision the marker names -- so anyone holding the checkout can rebuild every
picture the paper shows, and a picture can never quietly disagree with the numbers beside it.

    python scripts/paper_figures.py --rev <sha>          # rewrite the blocks in docs/paper.md
    python scripts/paper_figures.py --check              # exit 1 if any block would change
    python scripts/paper_figures.py --emit DIR           # one .tex spec per figure, for a figure lab

Sub-doctrine 12.e: the toil of keeping a picture in step with its data is automated, and the
`--check` mode is the check that says out loud when the step was missed. The history figures
are pinned to a revision (`rev:` in the marker) so the check is deterministic; in a shallow
clone the pinned revision cannot be walked, and the check says so instead of pretending.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

